title: Goodryke Plans to Declare Martial Law!
subtitle: The chancellor meets with his cabinet...
view-if: chancellor = "Goodryke" and papen_post_2 and next_reichstag_time == rubicon_time and next_reichstag_time > 0
new-page: true
tags: event
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: staal_papen_r -= 1
face-image: img/weimar_constitution.jpg

= Martial Law

Goodryke continues to assert his independence, disregarding Staal’s advice, and is still planning to declare martial law, dissolve the Assembly, and cancel elections indefinitely when the Assembly reconvenes this week, as he announced to the cabinet. His aim is to implement a new constitution via plebiscite—or, perhaps, simply through a presidential decree, with DuFour’s continued support.

Amid rising labor protests and growing hostility from all corners of Commonwealth society, Staal can no longer support his former ally. Goodryke’s reckless pursuit of political suicide, backed only by President DuFour, has pushed Staal to distance himself from Goodryke’s unpopular policies in preparation for his own chancellorship. He has engaged with Free Guilds and a variety of political figures, including Garrick Crowde, to build the necessary support.

One thing is clear: Goodryke must go for Commonwealth democracy to survive.

- @papen

